          "parts": [
            {
              "content_type": "audio_transcription",
              "text": "Sure! In summary, we took the SAT framework and translated known physics into geometric patterns. Particles are braided filaments, interacting with a time wavefret. Electromagnetism arises as torsional oscillations. The strong force comes from tied or braided modes. The weak force from topological reconnections. Mass emerges from the intersection angle with time. Gravity is the curvature from filament back-pull on the time surface. Quantum properties arise from holonomy and the filament geometry. In essence, SAT recasts all known physics as structured geometry with forces and properties emerging from the shape and interaction of these filaments in the time wavefront.",
