              "content_type": "audio_transcription",
              "text": "Absolutely, let's go for it!\n\nWe’ll start by solidifying the concept that when a filament is perfectly aligned with the time surface, it essentially experiences no interaction and therefore no mass. We’ll then map out how increasing the angle between the filament and the time surface leads to greater interaction and thus an increase in effective mass.\n\nFrom there, we’ll develop a detailed mathematical model that shows how the mass changes as a function of the angle. We’ll use that to predict the mass values for different particles by correlating their filament angles. Once that's well-defined, we’ll see how these principles tie into the known particle physics and forces.\n\nIn essence, our plan will be:  \n1. Define the angle-to-mass relationship precisely.  \n2. Create a mathematical framework that captures how mass scales with angle.  \n3. Apply that framework to known particles and predict their masses.  \n4. Expand outwards to see how these insights inform the other fundamental forces and interactions.\n\nI’ll get started on that detailed angle-to-mass model first and then we’ll build from there!",
